{"abstract":"Transformation of the urban context is a continuous process of change, in which different interests and forms of rationality are converging. It is often the ground for agonistic forces that negotiate their values, projects and future views. (Concilio & Tosoni, 2018; Mouffe, 2000). However, in relevant innovation processes, such as urban or large scale projects, a design approach is crucial, as it helps to stay on course towards the ultimate purpose of the whole innovation process. In many urban innovation processes however, this approach is often overshadowed by considerations related to administrative or operative issues. This paper is based on the experience in an ongoing EU project, Climaborough, which is promoting a number of innovative initiatives in 12 European pilot cities in a Net Zero perspective. The first learning from this project highlights the designer’s role in foregrounding the value of design in an innovative project. It does so by defining a design-based innovation process to promote initiatives for urban innovation. The paper will describe the three phases of the process: challenge definition, innovative procurement process and experimental sandbox and propose reflections on how the knowledge coming from those phases can be distilled, replicated and reused.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Morelli, Nicola","Colclough, Graham","Neuhoff, Rike","Simeone, Luca","Starostka, Justyna","Zohar, Hadas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-770484"],"event":{"end":"2024-05-17","place":"Budapest, hu","start":"2024-05-15","title":"Cumulus Budapest 2024","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Morelli, Nicola"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","UrbanDNA"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"bridging by design a designerly approach for cities to support innovation processes in the urban context","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/756101185/Bridging_by_design.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-770484","ids":["aau-716cfa9f-9444-461c-a3fc-3e8f459b7d77"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-DD9AEE7C2E0C4187D6C48837FB57DC4D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/756101185/Bridging_by_design.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Section for Industrial Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Section for Media Technology - Campus Copenhagen","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Service Systems Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"urbandna","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"UrbanDNA","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Nicola","key":"morellipau","last":"Morelli","locid":"661d9255-325e-48fb-93a0-a09d52fa9c6e","name":"Morelli, Nicola","orcid":"0000-0002-7056-4421","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Graham","key":"colcloughpau","last":"Colclough","name":"Colclough, Graham","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rike","key":"neuhoffpau","last":"Neuhoff","locid":"2c453c44-1cb3-4875-92d7-5005eb289729","name":"Neuhoff, Rike","orcid":"0000-0002-2448-1844","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Luca","key":"simeonepau","last":"Simeone","locid":"a4374675-6d6b-4886-b088-e943964db21a","name":"Simeone, Luca","orcid":"0000-0003-0527-3270","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Justyna","key":"starostkapau","last":"Starostka","name":"Starostka, Justyna","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hadas","key":"zoharpau","last":"Zohar","locid":"0b932395-7ad3-481f-b47d-e189ea6624be","name":"Zohar, Hadas","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["2490046X"],"place":"Moholy-Nagy University of Art and Design, Budapest","publisher":"Aalto University","series":"Cumulus Conference Proceedings Series","status":"p","subtitle":"P/References of Design","title":"Cumulus Conference Proceedings"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-716cfa9f-9444-461c-a3fc-3e8f459b7d77"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"BRIDGING BY DESIGN. A DESIGNERLY APPROACH FOR CITIES TO SUPPORT INNOVATION PROCESSES IN THE URBAN CONTEXT","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-770484","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Transformation of the urban context is a continuous process of change, in which different interests and forms of rationality are converging. It is often the ground for agonistic forces that negotiate their values, projects and future views. (Concilio & Tosoni, 2018; Mouffe, 2000). However, in relevant innovation processes, such as urban or large scale projects, a design approach is crucial, as it helps to stay on course towards the ultimate purpose of the whole innovation process. In many urban innovation processes however, this approach is often overshadowed by considerations related to administrative or operative issues. This paper is based on the experience in an ongoing EU project, Climaborough, which is promoting a number of innovative initiatives in 12 European pilot cities in a Net Zero perspective. The first learning from this project highlights the designer’s role in foregrounding the value of design in an innovative project. It does so by defining a design-based innovation process to promote initiatives for urban innovation. The paper will describe the three phases of the process: challenge definition, innovative procurement process and experimental sandbox and propose reflections on how the knowledge coming from those phases can be distilled, replicated and reused.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Morelli, Nicola","Colclough, Graham","Neuhoff, Rike","Simeone, Luca","Starostka, Justyna","Zohar, Hadas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-808924"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Urban DNA"],"keyword":["Design facilitation","Net zero","Procurement process","Sandbox","Urban innovation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"bridging by design a designerly approach for cities to support innovation processes in the urban context","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/files/756101185/Bridging_by_design.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-808924","ids":["itu-b6a85780-8173-4d32-b9ee-1f47a10f784e"],"keyword":["Design facilitation","Net Zero","Procurement process,","Sandbox","Urban Innovation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-22641DCB19593608291374B9292B4C8E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/files/756101185/Bridging_by_design.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"urban dna","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Urban DNA","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Audio-Visual Computing","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Media, Art & Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nicola","key":"morellipau","last":"Morelli","name":"Morelli, Nicola","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Graham","key":"colcloughpau","last":"Colclough","name":"Colclough, Graham","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rike","key":"neuhoffpau","last":"Neuhoff","name":"Neuhoff, Rike","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Luca","key":"simeonepau","last":"Simeone","name":"Simeone, Luca","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Justyna","key":"starostkapau","last":"Starostka","locid":"41da2096-dc8b-44c2-93ad-6473e220f85e","name":"Starostka, Justyna","orcid":"0000-0002-8087-3981","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hadas","key":"zoharpau","last":"Zohar","name":"Zohar, Hadas","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9789527549025"],"status":"p","title":"P/References of Design, Cumulus Conference Proceedings Budapest 2024"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-b6a85780-8173-4d32-b9ee-1f47a10f784e"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Bridging by Design. A Designerly Approach for Cities to Support Innovation Processes in the Urban Context","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-808924","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"As urban policy and governance challenges become increasingly complex, interdisciplinary approaches and participatory methodologies are essential. The evolving role of design affects the way it is practiced in these contexts. Instead of solely providing solutions, designers are now expected to connect, navigate, and facilitate collaboration between stakeholders from different public sector organizations. This paper aims to explore how multi-organizational design facilitation can contribute to addressing complex urban challenges, fostering and accelerating adoption of sustainable solutions. We delve into three concepts that underpin the creative facilitation process: the design mindset, futures thinking and experimental attitude. The context of this study is a big European project in which 12 cities collaborate and experiment, aiming to solve specific urban challenges. The paper argues for design facilitation to bridge gaps between diverse stakeholders, encourage co-creation, and facilitate the development of innovative solutions across various parties.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Starostka, Justyna","Neuhoff, Rike","Morelli, Nicola","Simeone, Luca"],"cuid":["S02-086.40-755760"],"event":{"end":"2024-06-28","place":"Boston","start":"2024-06-23","title":"Design Research Society Conference","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2024-09","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Cities","Design","Design facilitation","Facilitation","Sustainable transition","Sustainable transitions"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"design facilitation navigating complexity for collaborative solutions to urban sustainability challenges","src":["aau","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.21606/drs.2024.500","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-086.40-755760","ids":["aau-0b1f1c8e-cfba-4fb3-a6b3-597a297dae0d","itu-e5425c83-7878-4b19-b4c3-a9a3c22f4946"],"keyword":["Cities","Design","Design facilitation","Facilitation","Sustainable transitions","sustainable transition"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-838F3B40F521014DA68C3C61224E6BD6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.21606/drs.2024.500","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/728607714/Navigating_complexity_design_facilitation_for_collaborative_solu.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Audio-Visual Computing","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Media, Art & Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Section for Media Technology - Campus Copenhagen","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Service Systems Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Justyna","key":"starostkapau","last":"Starostka","locid":"41da2096-dc8b-44c2-93ad-6473e220f85e","name":"Starostka, Justyna","orcid":"0000-0002-8087-3981","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rike","key":"neuhoffpau","last":"Neuhoff","locid":"2c453c44-1cb3-4875-92d7-5005eb289729","name":"Neuhoff, Rike","orcid":"0000-0002-2448-1844","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Nicola","key":"morellipau","last":"Morelli","locid":"661d9255-325e-48fb-93a0-a09d52fa9c6e","name":"Morelli, Nicola","orcid":"0000-0002-7056-4421","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Luca","key":"simeonepau","last":"Simeone","locid":"a4374675-6d6b-4886-b088-e943964db21a","name":"Simeone, Luca","orcid":"0000-0003-0527-3270","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.21606/drs.2024.500","edition":"2024","eisbn":["9781912294626"],"place":"Boston","publisher":"Design Research Society","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of DRS2024","volume":"DRS"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-0b1f1c8e-cfba-4fb3-a6b3-597a297dae0d","itu-e5425c83-7878-4b19-b4c3-a9a3c22f4946"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Design facilitation: Navigating complexity for collaborative solutions to urban sustainability challenges","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-086.40-755760","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"In recent years, design in the public sector has gained popularity amongst policymakers as well as among scholars. Design is perceived as a promising way to create more successful policies and public services. Despite growing popularity, a critical reflection on benefits and challenges, as well as about different understandings of design practices in the public sector, are still lacking. Therefore, this paper aims to investigate different ways public organizations engage and introduce design approach. In this paper we present 3 municipalities in Denmark and the way design is understood and implemented in organizational work practices. Our contribution to theory is twofold. First, our research responds to the recent call of different researchers to investigate how design is operationalized and drawn upon in practice by different organizations in the public sector. Second, our research contributes to the design field, by showing barriers of implementations, different benefits and challenges connected with design in organizations with no prior experience in design.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Starostka, Justyna","Götzen, Amalia De","Morelli, Nicola"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-686810"],"event":{"end":"2023-06-29","place":"Toronto, ca","start":"2023-06-27","title":"The 6th International Conference on Public Policy","year":"2023"},"filters":{"added":"2023-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"design facilitation in public sector learnings from public libraries in denmark","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.ippapublicpolicy.org/conference/icpp6-toronto-2023/panel-list/17/panel/design-led-policy-and-governance-in-practice-a-global-perspective/1386","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-686810","ids":["aau-7a89583f-8a2e-4c5c-8e47-e9e8c98ba0e3"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-37ADDA32105430D3BAF1D179057F9235"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Section for Media Technology - Campus Copenhagen","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Service Systems Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Justyna","key":"starostkapau","last":"Starostka","locid":"1979e390-c344-465a-a57a-69b3794b7f42","name":"Starostka, Justyna","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Amalia","key":"degötzenpau","last":"de Götzen","locid":"3e5ee7f6-ec4c-4cca-a8ba-749ffd5f8f17","name":"Götzen, Amalia De","name_org":"de Götzen, Amalia","orcid":"0000-0001-7214-5856","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Nicola","key":"morellipau","last":"Morelli","locid":"661d9255-325e-48fb-93a0-a09d52fa9c6e","name":"Morelli, Nicola","orcid":"0000-0002-7056-4421","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"place":"Toronto, Canada","status":"p","title":"The 6th International Conference on Public Policy (ICPP6), Toronto Metropolitan University's Faculty of Arts and Public Policy, 27-29th June 2023"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-7a89583f-8a2e-4c5c-8e47-e9e8c98ba0e3"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Design facilitation in public sector – learnings from public libraries in Denmark","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-686810","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Using a wider context of a growing role of service design (SD) in different change processes, the aim of this article is to explore the transformative role of service design on two levels: organizational and societal. We investigated a transformation process of a public sector organization – a public library, showing how service design can be a vehicle of organizational and societal changes. We were able to map 3 cycles of transition that have been gradually expanding the visions, theories of change, mindsets, and new ways of designing in the organization, helping to achieve more and more agency in transforming, first the organization, and then local community. The article contributes to the growing body of knowledge connecting design with change. It also creates a more in-depth understanding of how SD can become a vehicle for transformation in a public sector organization.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Starostka, Justyna","Morelli, Nicola","Götzen, Amalia De"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-686861"],"event":{"end":"2023-07-14","place":"Rio De Janeiro, br","start":"2023-07-11","title":"ServDes 2023","year":"2023"},"filters":{"added":"2023-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Public library","Service Design"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the transformative role of service design a case study of a public library","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3384/ecp203001","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-686861","ids":["aau-892b74cd-43b0-47c2-9ddc-9c69bb454465"],"keyword":["Design for Policy","Public Library","Service Design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-B092C1D3488747746B53AA1D32BF8FF2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3384/ecp203001","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/614533449/ServDes_2023_paper_219_The_transformative_role_of_service_design_a_case_study_of_a_public_library_AJUSTADO.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Section for Media Technology - Campus Copenhagen","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Service Systems Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Justyna","key":"starostkapau","last":"Starostka","locid":"1979e390-c344-465a-a57a-69b3794b7f42","name":"Starostka, Justyna","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Nicola","key":"morellipau","last":"Morelli","locid":"661d9255-325e-48fb-93a0-a09d52fa9c6e","name":"Morelli, Nicola","orcid":"0000-0002-7056-4421","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Amalia","key":"degötzenpau","last":"de Götzen","locid":"3e5ee7f6-ec4c-4cca-a8ba-749ffd5f8f17","name":"Götzen, Amalia De","name_org":"de Götzen, Amalia","orcid":"0000-0001-7214-5856","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Carla","key":"cipollapedh","last":"Cipolla","name":"Cipolla, Carla","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Claudia","key":"montalvãopedh","last":"Mont’Alvão","name":"Mont’Alvão, Claudia","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Larissa","key":"fariaspedh","last":"Farias","name":"Farias, Larissa","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Manuela","key":"quaresmapedh","last":"Quaresma","name":"Quaresma, Manuela","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3384/ecp203001","eisbn":["9789180754767"],"issn":["16503686"],"pages":"28-43","place":"Rio de Janeiro","publisher":"Linköping University Electronic Press","series":"Linköping Electronic Conference Proceedings","status":"p","subtitle":"Entanglements and Flows. Service Encounters and Meanings. Conference Proceedings","title":"ServDes 2023"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","sdg":["10. Reduced Inequalities","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-892b74cd-43b0-47c2-9ddc-9c69bb454465"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"The transformative role of service design – a case study of a public library","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-686861","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Public libraries are more and more recognized to become partners in co-design and technology education, also aiming to bridge the digital divide. We see it as a great opportunity to expand the roles of public libraries even further, engaging citizens in co-design processes, improving existing public e-services and co-designing new services. That shift requires new roles taken by librarians, but also new processes, as well as new methods of development of e-services in the public sector. In PDC Place Nordic we explore this new role of libraries in participatory future making, engaging librarians, academics, practitioners, and different local communities. Events will take place in Copenhagen, Malmö, and Helsinki/Espoo.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Götzen, Amalia De","Starostka, Justyna","Saad-Sulonen, Joanna","Ehrenberg, Nils","Linde, Per"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-069178"],"event":{"end":"2022-09-01","place":"Newcastle upon Tyne, gb","start":"2022-08-19","title":"Participatory Design Conference 2022","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2022-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Finland","Sweden"],"glorg":["Aalto University","All Global Affiliations","Malmö University"],"keyword":["Libraries","Participatory Design","Public Digitalization","Public services"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pdc place nordic participatory design in for the digitalization of public services","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85137155693&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-069178","identifier":[{"id":"85137155693","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-421b6339-dd8f-4876-9a3f-2bbf2011d018"],"keyword":["Participatory design","libraries","public digitalization","public services"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2A06414E7125ECA90BFFF97E61820C06"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Section for Media Technology - Campus Copenhagen","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Service Systems Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"fi","key":"aalto university","loc":["Finland","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Aalto University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"se","key":"malmö university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Malmö University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Amalia","key":"degötzenpau","last":"De Götzen","locid":"3e5ee7f6-ec4c-4cca-a8ba-749ffd5f8f17","name":"Götzen, Amalia De","name_org":"De Götzen, Amalia","orcid":"0000-0001-7214-5856","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Justyna","key":"starostkapau","last":"Starostka","locid":"1979e390-c344-465a-a57a-69b3794b7f42","name":"Starostka, Justyna","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Joanna","key":"saadsulonenpau","last":"Saad-Sulonen","name":"Saad-Sulonen, Joanna","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Nils","key":"ehrenbergpau","last":"Ehrenberg","name":"Ehrenberg, Nils","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Per","key":"lindepau","last":"Linde","name":"Linde, Per","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3537797.3537885","eisbn":["9781450396813"],"pages":"286-287","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery (ACM)","status":"p","title":"PDC '22: Proceedings of the Participatory Design Conference 2022","volume":"2"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85137155693"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-421b6339-dd8f-4876-9a3f-2bbf2011d018"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"PDC Place Nordic : participatory design in/for the digitalization of public services","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-069178","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"In recent years, design in the public sector has gained popularity amongst policymakers as well as among scholars. Design is perceived as a promising way to create more successful policies and public services. Out of many different approaches, design thinking (DT) has become significantly popular, as it promises to deal with wicked problems in a new way. Despite growing popularity, however, a critical reflection on benefits and challenges, as well as about different understandings of DT practices in public sector, are still lacking. Therefore, this paper aims to investigate different ways public organisations engage and introduce DT. In this paper we present 3 different municipalities in Denmark and the way design and DT is understood and implemented in organizational work practices. Our contribution to theory is twofold. First, our research responds to the recent call of different researchers to investigate how DT is operationalised and drawn upon in practice by different organizations in the public sector. Second, our research contributes to the design field, by showing barriers of implementations, different benefits and challenges connected with design implementation in organisations with no prior experience in design.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Starostka, Justyna","Götzen, Amalia De"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-081899"],"event":{"end":"2022-07-02","place":"Bilbao, es","start":"2022-06-25","title":"Design Research Society Conference 2022","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2022-07","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Co creation","Design","Design science","Design thinking","Public administration","Public policy"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"what a designer does in a municipality different approaches towards design in three danish municipalities","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.21606/drs.2022.517","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-081899","ids":["aau-6d7fc251-e027-44d4-b14a-8f8a2321f773"],"keyword":["co-creation","design","design science","design thinking","public administration","public policy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-63AB72E46F55749304B156557EC6144F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.21606/drs.2022.517","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/482467427/_What_a_designer_does_in_a_municipality_Different_approaches_to.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Section for Media Technology - Campus Copenhagen","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Service Systems Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Justyna","key":"starostkapau","last":"Starostka","locid":"1979e390-c344-465a-a57a-69b3794b7f42","name":"Starostka, Justyna","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Amalia","key":"degötzenpau","last":"De Götzen","locid":"3e5ee7f6-ec4c-4cca-a8ba-749ffd5f8f17","name":"Götzen, Amalia De","name_org":"De Götzen, Amalia","orcid":"0000-0001-7214-5856","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.21606/drs.2022.517","eisbn":["9781912294572"],"issn":["23983132"],"publisher":"Design Research Society","series":"Proceedings of DRS","status":"p","title":"DRS2022: Bilbao"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-6d7fc251-e027-44d4-b14a-8f8a2321f773"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"“What a designer does in a municipality?” – different approaches towards design in three Danish municipalities","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-081899","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"In recent years, design in the public sector has gained popularity amongst policymakers as well as among scholars. Design is perceived as a promising way to create more successful policies and public services. Despite growing popularity, a critical reflection on benefits and challenges, as well as about different understandings of design practices in the public sector, are still lacking. Therefore, this paper aims to investigate different ways public organizations engage and introduce design approach. In this paper we present 3 municipalities in Denmark and the way design is understood and implemented in organizational work practices. Our contribution to theory is twofold. First, our research responds to the recent call of different researchers to investigate how design is operationalized and drawn upon in practice by different organizations in the public sector. Second, our research contributes to the design field, by showing barriers of implementations, different benefits and challenges connected with design in organizations with no prior experience in design.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Starostka, Justyna","Götzen, Amalia De","Morelli, Nicola"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-120099"],"filters":{"added":"2022-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Co creation","Design","Design science","Design thinking","Public administration","Public policy"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"design thinking in the public sector a case study of three danish municipalities","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/25741292.2022.2144817","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-120099","identifier":[{"id":"85142166826","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-f0f15ac2-9f53-4ab9-be9d-8665defd8bed"],"keyword":["Design","co-creation","design science","design thinking","public administration","public policy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0F674600527BD59582BE8F785063DC99"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/25741292.2022.2144817","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/514425913/Design_thinking_in_the_public_sector_a_case_study_of_three_Danish_municipalities.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Section for Media Technology - Campus Copenhagen","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Service Systems Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Justyna","key":"starostkapau","last":"Starostka","locid":"1979e390-c344-465a-a57a-69b3794b7f42","name":"Starostka, Justyna","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Amalia","key":"degötzenpau","last":"de Götzen","locid":"3e5ee7f6-ec4c-4cca-a8ba-749ffd5f8f17","name":"Götzen, Amalia De","name_org":"de Götzen, Amalia","orcid":"0000-0001-7214-5856","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Nicola","key":"morellipau","last":"Morelli","locid":"661d9255-325e-48fb-93a0-a09d52fa9c6e","name":"Morelli, Nicola","orcid":"0000-0002-7056-4421","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/25741292.2022.2144817","issn":["25741292"],"issue":"4","journal":"Policy Design and Practice","pages":"504-515","publisher":"Taylor & Francis","status":"p","title":"Policy Design and Practice","volume":"5"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85142166826"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-f0f15ac2-9f53-4ab9-be9d-8665defd8bed"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Design thinking in the public sector – a case study of three Danish municipalities","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-120099","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Although the body of research on design thinking (DT) is growing, knowledge regarding DT facilitation in innovation projects is sparse. Through explorative case studies, we explore how facilitators understand and apply DT to innovation projects. Our findings reveal that different DT facilitators take markedly polar different approaches to DT facilitation. We advance the DT literature by establishing links with the group facilitation literature and developing a taxonomy of DT facilitation anchored by two opposite approaches to DT facilitation: a method approach and a cofacilitation approach. Our findings demonstrate that different interpretations of DT can lead to different facilitation practices. This insight is valuable for innovation project owners who hire DT facilitators, the research community and facilitators themselves.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Starostka, Justyna","Evald, Majbritt Rostgaard","Clarke, Ann Højbjerg","Hansen, Per Richard"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-000474"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Starostka, Justyna"],"keyword":["Design thinking","Group facilitation","Innovation projects","cofacilitation approach","design thinking facilitation","design thinking practice","method approach"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"taxonomy of design thinking facilitation","src":["aau","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/189850446/caim.12451.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The study this article is based upon is part of a larger project that has received funding from the European Regional Development Fund (ERDF) under the European Structural and Investment Fund (ESI) 2014–2020 (Grant RFD‐15‐0021). We would like to thank the ERDF for making this possible. Also, we would like to express our special thanks to the reviewers and editor of CIM who saw the potential and helped us develop the paper."],"id":"S02-100.00-000474","identifier":[{"id":"85111841148","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-09169e59-67b0-473f-9919-dce69a1844a4","sdu-80ab4e33-784e-4df5-872c-71203aa58f48"],"keyword":["cofacilitation approach","design thinking","design thinking facilitation","design thinking practice","group facilitation","innovation projects","method approach"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-EFB8CE09E664011336564801507DA33D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/189850446/caim.12451.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/517878233/caim.12451.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Section for Media Technology - Campus Copenhagen","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Service Systems Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university o